# The message box (Yes/No, Ok, Ok/Cancel, ...): a 640 x 400 dialog centred on a 40% scrim. MessageBoxParent is the box
# and is drawn as the dialog panel itself (gogoMessageBox may move it, e.g. the resolution prompt in a corner), its
# children ride along. The button slots: gogoMessageBox reads the positions of ButtonOk (slot 1), ButtonNo (slot 2) and
# ButtonCancel (slot 3) and moves the buttons it shows into them, Yes into slot 1 and a lone No into slot 3, so slot 1 is
# at the right (the primary action) and slot 3 at the left. The unnamed title bar box is matched by its legacy rect
# before the parent moves.
hide at:252,100,552,150
scrim
window $MessageBoxParent centre middle 0 0 640 400 dialog
window $StaticTextTitle left top 664 364 592 32 section
window $StaticTextMessage left top 664 412 592 220 body
window $ButtonCancel left top 664 672 180 44 button
window $ButtonNo left top 870 672 180 44 button
window $ButtonOk left top 1076 672 180 44 primary
window $ButtonYes left top 1076 672 180 44 primary
